@page
@model Matcad.Pages.Settings.ConnectionsModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Connections";
    ViewData["PageSub"] = "What Matcad gets from other apps and what it gives them.";
    ViewData["Crumbs"] = Crumbs.Of(("Settings", "/Settings"), ("Connections", null));
}

<p class="mat-muted">
    Matcad makes apps reachable (<code>web.route</code>): Mattiverse binds every app it installs, and each binding is a route to the app under its
    name of the domain or, without a domain, on a port of its own, listed here and on the <a asp-page="/Routes/Index">Routes</a> page. A route needs a
    host or a port and the app's address, which a name alone does not give: without Mattiverse, add the route on the Routes page.
</p>

<mat-connections />
